  "behaviorVerified": [
    "An explicit host reference selects answer mode even when the host question has no trailing question mark.",
    "Exact leading/trailing whitespace, newlines, combining Unicode, emoji, and values beyond the old conversation limit are preserved in referenced requests with empty conversation history.",
    "Two successive questions attach their own originating task references and distinct answer task IDs.",
    "Secure storage receives the exact encoded body before send; ambiguous delivery, manual retry, and app relaunch reuse the same bytes and task ID even after the original reference expires, allowing the host to replay an existing result.",
    "Empty or oversized input and secure-save failure send nothing, do not truncate the payload, and retain the pending question; the view keeps the draft unless sendPrompt accepts it.",
    "Unclaimed questions expire after their bounded deadline or session stop. Expired answers cannot fall back to ordinary tasks; Start a new request clears both reference and legacy conversation selection.",
    "Malformed structured and wrong-task replies cannot create a new answer context; cancelled and completed requests cannot promote question-looking text into later task context.",
    "Legacy clarification and Mail privacy behavior remain available for unreferenced hosts; scoped answers never borrow that history.",
    "An old expiry timer cannot invalidate an answer already durably claimed for delivery."
  ],
